cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use Tesserae, please cite the project as below. To cite a specific
  earlier version, cite its author (Tesserae V3: Chris Forstall; Tesserae V1:
  Poornima Shakthi).
title: "Tesserae V6: Intertextual and Literary Discovery"
abstract: >-
  Tesserae is an intertextual analysis tool for discovering textual parallels
  (allusions, echoes, borrowings) in Latin, Greek, English, and other classical
  and ancient-language corpora.
type: software
version: "6.0"
# First V6 commit. Adjust if a formal public release date is preferred.
date-released: "2026-01-29"
license: MIT
url: "https://tesserae.caset.buffalo.edu"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tesserae/tesserae-v6"
authors:
  - family-names: Coffee
    given-names: Neil
    affiliation: "University at Buffalo, SUNY"
  - family-names: Scheirer
    given-names: Walter
    affiliation: "University of Notre Dame"
keywords:
  - intertextuality
  - classical philology
  - Latin
  - Greek
  - digital humanities
  - text reuse detection

